WEBVTT

00:01:30.621 --> 00:01:34.571
"O sleep, O gentle sleep,
nature's soft nurse,

00:01:34.595 --> 00:01:35.920
how have I frighted thee?"

00:01:35.944 --> 00:01:38.517
Shakespeare again, from --
I won't say it --

00:01:38.541 --> 00:01:39.915
the Scottish play.

00:01:39.939 --> 00:01:41.190
(Laughter)

00:01:42.577 --> 00:01:43.807
From the same time:

00:01:43.831 --> 00:01:48.036
"Sleep is the golden chain
that ties health and our bodies together."

00:01:48.060 --> 00:01:52.239
Extremely prophetic, by Thomas Dekker,
another Elizabethan dramatist.

00:01:52.636 --> 00:01:55.654
But if we jump forward 400 years,

00:01:55.678 --> 00:01:59.019
the tone about sleep changes somewhat.

00:01:59.043 --> 00:02:02.214
This is from Thomas Edison,
from the beginning of the 20th century: